                <pb facs="0651" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2815: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-23T11:00:00-05:00">November 23, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>430. For Minister Johnson at Nanking: Your 983, November 22, 1 p.m. As yet the
                    Department has not been approached with such a request, but it approves the
                    sending of the Military Attaché to Chinchow for observation as proposed by you,
                    without reference to such a request and in regular course.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
